From: jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0022] HlmsPbs: geometric specular anti-aliasing for normal-mapped surfaces

MEDIA-ONLY (Studio restages media; every tree needs the patch loop). Folds the
screen-space variance of the final shading normal into the GGX alpha (Kaplanyan
2016; Unity HDRP / Unreal defaults 0.25 / 0.18), gated on normal_map_tex so
untextured normals and flat maps are bit-identical. Cures the mip-collapse glints
("white dots") on low-roughness normal-mapped materials at distance. Toksvig is
not available on this pin: getTSNormal reconstructs Z so |n| is always 1.

--- a/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any
+++ b/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any
@@ -843,6 +843,35 @@
 			@property( normal_map )
 				pixelData.normal = normalize( mul( TBN, pixelData.normal ) );
 			@end
+			@property( normal_map_tex )
+				// JAHSHAKA patch 0022 - GEOMETRIC SPECULAR ANTI-ALIASING (Kaplanyan 2016,
+				// the Unity HDRP / Unreal runtime form). A normal map's detail collapses
+				// through its mip chain while the roughness does not widen to match, so a
+				// low-roughness normal-mapped surface sparkles at distance (the owner's
+				// 'white dots'). The screen-space derivatives of the FINAL shading normal
+				// measure how fast it turns across a pixel; that variance is folded into
+				// the GGX alpha. Zero on a flat surface with a flat map (bit-identical),
+				// gated on normal_map_tex so untextured normals never move. Constants are
+				// Unity's defaults: screen-space variance 0.25, threshold 0.18.
+				{
+					midf3 jahNddx = midf3_c( OGRE_ddx( pixelData.normal ) );
+					midf3 jahNddy = midf3_c( OGRE_ddy( pixelData.normal ) );
+					midf jahVariance = _h( 0.25 ) * ( dot( jahNddx, jahNddx ) + dot( jahNddy, jahNddy ) );
+					midf jahKernel = min( _h( 2.0 ) * jahVariance, _h( 0.18 ) );
+					if( jahKernel > _h( 0.0 ) )
+					{
+					@property( perceptual_roughness )
+						// pixelData.roughness is the GGX alpha here.
+						pixelData.roughness = sqrt( pixelData.roughness * pixelData.roughness + jahKernel );
+					@else
+						// pixelData.roughness is perceptual: alpha = r*r.
+						midf jahAlpha = pixelData.roughness * pixelData.roughness;
+						pixelData.roughness = sqrt( sqrt( jahAlpha * jahAlpha + jahKernel ) );
+					@end
+						pixelData.roughness = min( pixelData.roughness, _h( 1.0 ) );
+					}
+				}
+			@end
 
 			@insertpiece( DoDirectionalShadowMaps )
 
